--- !u!114 &2884922084475175736
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6763988370665486853}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9541d86e2fd84c1d9990edf0852d74ab, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>What''s happening:</b>

    Before a mesh can be drawn by the GPU,
    the CPU needs to prepare the information. However, since the CPU and GPU are
    different hardware components, there is a lot of overhead per ''draw call'' command
    that is being sent. This is often a major cause for performance issues.



    <b>How
    to measure it:</b>

    The basic measurable value is called draw calls. There
    is usually one draw call for each material per mesh. The CPU can also save some
    of them by batching. So the main value are Batches.

    - <100 Batches: Extremely
    well optimized

    - <300 Batches: Suitable for mobile use

    - <500 Batches:
    Suitable for Quest 3 headsets

    - ~2000 Batches: Still works well on PCs

    -
    >10''000 Batches: Often very noticeable performance problems.



    <b>How to
    improve it:</b>

    - Manually combining meshes and materials: The fewer meshes
    and materials there are, the fewer number of draw calls there are in the end.

    -
    Static batching: If a mesh is set to static, you''re promising that the mesh
    won''t move. Therefore, the CPU can combine static meshes with the same material
    into one.

    - GPU instancing: The CPU is able to tell the GPU to draw the
    same mesh multiple times. This allows to draw foliage like grass or trees very
    efficiently.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
